        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "bbox": [
            0.098,
            0.139,
            0.221,
            0.157
          ],
          "level": 2,
          "content": "Activity 2 :"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.096,
            0.164,
            0.9,
            0.203
          ],
          "content": "Divide the students of your class into three groups and ask each group to do one of the following activities."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.119,
            0.208,
            0.902,
            0.266
          ],
          "content": "1. Collect the marks obtained by all the students of your class in Mathematics in the latest examination conducted by your school. Form a grouped frequency distribution of the data obtained."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.118,
            0.272,
            0.901,
            0.312
          ],
          "content": "2. Collect the daily maximum temperatures recorded for a period of 30 days in your city. Present this data as a grouped frequency table."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.118,
            0.316,
            0.901,
            0.356
          ],
          "content": "3. Measure the heights of all the students of your class (in cm) and form a grouped frequency distribution table of this data."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.096,
            0.361,
            0.902,
            0.421
          ],
          "content": "After all the groups have collected the data and formed grouped frequency distribution tables, the groups should find the mean in each case by the method which they find appropriate."
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "bbox": [
            0.403,
            0.445,
            0.595,
            0.464
          ],
          "level": 2,
          "content": "EXERCISE 13.1"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.125,
            0.475,
            0.901,
            0.529
          ],
          "content": "**1.** A survey was conducted by a group of students as a part of their environment awareness programme, in which they collected the following data regarding the number of plants in 20 houses in a locality. Find the mean number of plants per house."
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "bbox": [
            0.162,
            0.532,
            0.883,
            0.595
          ],
          "content": "| Number of plants | 0 - 2 | 2 - 4 | 4 - 6 | 6 - 8 | 8 - 10 | 10 - 12 | 12 - 14 |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| Number of houses | 1 | 2 | 1 | 5 | 6 | 2 | 3 |",
          "captions": [],
          "footnotes": [],
          "image_source": "images/page_10_table_10.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.155,
            0.607,
            0.673,
            0.626
          ],
          "content": "Which method did you use for finding the mean, and why?"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.124,
            0.631,
            0.822,
            0.65
          ],
          "content": "**2.** Consider the following distribution of daily wages of 50 workers of a factory."
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "bbox": [
            0.162,
            0.659,
            0.883,
            0.723
          ],
          "content": "| Daily wages (in `) | 500 - 520 | 520 -540 | 540 - 560 | 560 - 580 | 580 -600 |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| Number of workers | 12 | 14 | 8 | 6 | 10 |",
          "captions": [],
          "footnotes": [],
          "image_source": "images/page_10_table_13.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.155,
            0.736,
            0.898,
            0.755
          ],
          "content": "Find the mean daily wages of the workers of the factory by using an appropriate method."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.125,
            0.759,
            0.899,
            0.796
          ],
          "content": "**3.** The following distribution shows the daily pocket allowance of children of a locality. The mean pocket allowance is Rs 18. Find the missing frequency f."
